      "body": "## Summary\n- Online SGLang capture now reads `model.draft_model_config` and `model.target_model_path` from the SpecForge Hydra file (or a Hydra override) instead of always using the Qwen3.5-4B draft layer ids.\n- `--skip-tokenizer-init` stays on by default and can be turned off with `specforge_online.skip_tokenizer_init` or `SKIP_TOKENIZER_INIT`, so a checkpoint that assigns `chat_template` during server load can initialize the tokenizer.\n- Drop the `--no-deps` tensorboard install from the light-deps script and smoke-check `torch.utils.tensorboard.SummaryWriter`.\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] Ran the online launch helpers locally (module is `pytest.mark.skip` in CI): Qwen layer ids still win when the recipe has no draft file, an explicit `capture_layer_ids` override still wins, a recipe draft JSON and `target_model_path` are picked up, and `skip_tokenizer_init: false` removes `--skip-tokenizer-init`.\n- [ ] Build the SpecForge image and confirm `smoke-check.sh` still passes, including the SummaryWriter import.\n\nMade with [Cursor](https://cursor.com)",
